Hi.

I am working on a problem in which I need to estimate players' impact on team performance (i.e., winning or losing a game).
For that, I have several attributes (measured as counts - e.g., goals scored, number of penalties generated, etc).

The main goals are:
1. To derive the factors associated with each position - the number of factors as well as their composition will vary according to players' positions;
2. To understand the impact of position on team performance;
3. To understand the impact of a specific player (which belongs to a specific playing position) on team performance.

For this, I implemented the following pipeline:
1. EFA and CFA for each playing position - I got three to four factors for each position (e.g., defense, kicking, etc.);
2. SEM with latent factors as predictors of team performance (i.e., win or loss);
3. Higher-order SEM in which the factors from the different playing positions are combined in a single model to predict team performance.

When implementing this pipeline, I am having some concerns, including (1) moderate factor loadings for the CFA models, (2) lack of convergence in the higher-order SEM (the different factors for each position are not sufficiently correlated).

Based on this, I have two main questions regarding this:
1. Does Lavaan handle latent variables that are reflected on count items (just like MPlus)?
2. Is it possible to accommodate formative models in Lavaan?
3. What do you think about the proposed analytical pipeline?

Thank you all in advance

Best regards,
Pedro

