Dear Yves and lavaan group,

I'm seeing what seems like strange behaviour in lavaan versions 0.5-23 and 0.6-1.1204, but which doesn't happen with version 0.5-22.

Here is one particular row of the output from standardizedSolution(), for the same data and the same code, for those three versions.

## lavaan 0.5-22 in R 3.3.1:
   lhs op rhs est.std    se       z pvalue
36  F1 ~~  F1   1.000 0.000      NA     NA

## lavaan 0.5-23 in R 3.4.3:
   lhs op rhs est.std    se            z pvalue
36  F1 ~~  F1   1.000 0.000 17957505.192  0.000

## lavaan 0.6-1.1204 in R 3.4.3:
   lhs op rhs est.std    se            z pvalue ci.lower ci.upper
36  F1 ~~  F1   1.000 0.000 35915010.440  0.000    1.000    1.000

F1 is an exogenous latent variable and I used std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE, so the output from version 0.5-22 is what I would expect.

Am I correct in thinking that z should be NA? If not, I would appreciate if someone could explain why. Other fixed parameters in the model have z = NA.

Code to reproduce this is given below.

Thanks,
Mark

