> Is it possible to use definition variables with lavaan? If not, is this on the roadmap?

Can you be more specific?  If you are referring to (e.g.) the ability to provide case-specific fixed loadings defined in rows of the data frame, then no, and I doubt it is in any way straight-forward to implement in lavaan because of its use of the parameter table.  You can do this in OpenMx, though.  If you are familiar with Bayesian software, you could also fit a more basic model in blavaan, save the JAGS or Stan syntax (without fitting the model), then update that syntax to use definition variables in place of specific fixed values.

