> I found the lavCor() function resulting in a pearson correlation matrix. I guess this was what I was looking for?

As Mikko pointed out, you can use the cor() function if all your variables are continuous.  lavCor() will do the same, but more flexibly.  If you declare any of your variables as ordered, it will return pearson correlations among numeric variables, polychoric correlations among ordered variables, and polyserial correlations between numeric and ordered variables.

