> 7            SMI   6   74 numeric   0    0   0.240      0.020    0
>
> 2. Where to start to solve this?

Well, you can divide Sand by 100, so that you can interpret effects in 100 units of Sand instead of 1 unit of Sand. Same with Silt and Clay.  And you could multiple SMI by 100, allowing you to interpret those effects in centi-units instead of units (if it is already a proportion, then this would be intuitive because you could interpret effects in terms of percentage-points, and 1-unit changes in the original variable would be the upper bound of possible change anyway).

